  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_asbest",
      "name": {
        "en": "Asbestos's Badge",
        "zh": "石棉证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_asbest",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Asbestos has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for preservation of the front while inflicting Arts casualties on the enemy.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Defender Operator during field operations to exercise Arts Protector responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员石棉擅长在维持战线的同时对敌人造成法术杀伤\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为重装干员，行使驭法铁卫职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_asbest",
      "name": {
        "en": "'Asbestos vs. Two-headed Gloompincer'",
        "zh": "“石棉大战双头钳兽”",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_asbest",
      "description": {
        "en": "To my young reader:\nHello, my young friend. I've seen the photograph you sent me, and read the letter attached to it. Luckily for you, your letter arrived during my return to Rim Billiton to write my next draft. But I am sorry to inform you that <i>Asbestos vs. Two-headed Gloompincer</i> is not one of my works. I did not write it. You profess your love for <i>Asbestos Tears Apart the Mutant Mangler</i>, but that was not written by me either. Those are unauthorized knock-offs.\nAs for <i>Asbestos Charges into the Cave of Death</i> and <i>Asbestos Conquers the Waterfall of Blood</i>... Yes, my editor says those two were actually mine. I'm sure my publisher has their reasons for choosing those sorts of names. I suppose otherwise I probably wouldn't have received your letter. Also, that sales tactic of 'buy the book for a complimentary miniature'... When my editor told me my books were incredibly popular among children, I was very confused, but now I understand.\nAfter receiving your letter, I went out to buy some of the Asbestos series, including the unauthorized volumes, and I noticed that, whether genuine or not, the free item was always a miniature. Did you make the board and other items in your photo yourself? You're amazing, reading my books as seriously as you have. As for your questions...\nYour first question about the color of Sami's Borea, that is, the aurora. While I've only seen and written about a green one, there are other colors such as red, violet, and blue. Your friend is right.\nAs for your second question, Sargonians really do use their tails for angling. According to them, there is even a species of sawtooth fin that has a special love for thin Archosauria tails, so only those blessed with such tails can catch them. You are right.\nOn the topic of your third question, whether the two-headed gloompincer or the mutant mangler would win in battle, I don't know about this. First of all, I have never seen either of them. Secondly, the two of them don't even appear in the same unauthorized book.\nWhich means you and your friend are equally matched. As for whether you two make up or not, that’s none of my business. That's something you'll have to do yourself. Also, there's no need to force him to 'seriously read the great hero Asbestos's books'. He'll read them if he's interested. I only wrote about my travels to record my experiences, impressions, and the sights I've seen. If you love them that much, I suggest you go see them for yourself. Who knows, maybe we'll run into each other. Maybe you'll be able to see even more than I have.\nFinally, I have included with my reply the Asbestos and Two-headed Gloompincer miniatures I got for free with those unauthorized volumes, which you can share with your friend. If you really want to make up with him, it'd probably be better to play with him than try to prove that you're right. Hope you enjoy your time with him.\nAh, yes, there's no use replying to this letter, since I'm setting off to Columbia tomorrow. I won't be able to receive it.",
        "zh": "答小读者：\n小朋友你好。你寄来的照片我看到了，信我也读了，算你运气好，你的信是在我回雷姆必拓写稿期间寄到的。不过很可惜，《石棉大战双头钳兽》并不是我的书，我没写过这个。虽然你说你很喜欢，但《石棉手撕变异裂兽》也不是我写的。这些都是盗版。\n至于《石棉勇闯夺命窟》《石棉征服血腥瀑布》……好吧，编辑说这两本确实是我的书。我猜出版社取这种名字有他们的道理，不然，可能我也不会收到你的信。还有那个“买书送棋子”的促销策略……之前编辑和我说我的书在儿童市场大受欢迎的时候我还有点纳闷，现在算是明白了。\n收到你的信之后，我自己也去买了几本“石棉系列”，盗版我也买了，发现无论是正版书还是盗版书，赠品都只有棋子。你照片里的棋盘和其他道具都是自己做的吧？你还挺厉害的，读我的书读得很认真嘛。至于你问的那几个问题……\n第一个问题，萨米“波利亚”——就是极光——的颜色。虽然我只见过，也只写过绿色的波利亚，但它是有其他颜色的，红色、紫色、蓝色，都有。你朋友说的没错。\n第二个问题，萨尔贡人确实会用尾巴钓鳞。按他们自己的说法，甚至有一种锯齿鳞还特别偏爱阿达克利斯的细尾巴，只有用细尾巴才能钓起来。你是对的。\n第三个问题，双头钳兽和变异裂兽哪个战斗力更强，这个我不知道。首先我没见过，其次这两个玩意儿甚至没在同一本盗版书里出场。\n所以，你和你的朋友打平了。至于你们要不要和好，我管不着，你自己解决。你也不用逼他“必须认真看石棉大英雄的书”，他爱看不看。我写游记，只是想记下我自己的经历、感受以及我看见的风景。如果你很喜欢那些风景，我建议你自己去看一看，说不定我们会在哪里碰上。或者，你能比我看见更多。\n最后，我把我买盗版书送的“石棉”和“双头钳兽”棋子寄给你，你可以赔给你的朋友。如果你真的很想和好，比起向他证明你才是对的，不如你们再开一局游戏。玩儿得开心。\n对了，不用给我回信，我明天就出发去哥伦比亚了，收不到。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ],
